  "about": "Raw measurements behind M5C.10e (docs/COVERAGE.md 'After batch 5', ADR-0166's M5C.10e amendment): how common is a let URL extended with += before a request (let url = ...; if (q) url += `?${q}`; fetch(url)), which before the fix made the let unknown (lets.ts read only plain x = v writes), so the request was DYNAMIC_URL. 'counts': GitHub REST GET /search/code (legacy engine, authenticated) total_count per query on 2026-11-06; the legacy engine drops punctuation, so the quoted phrases match token runs (let url, url, fetch url) and the counts only give scale. 'sample': the first 10 non-fork hits (one per repo) of each of the first two queries, each file read with GET /repos/<repo>/contents/<path> and parsed with TypeScript (never run). 'lets': each let whose name has a `x += ...` and is the first argument of a fetch/axios call, what each append starts with (null: not literal text), and 'queryOnly' (every append starts with ? or &, or the initializer holds a literal ?). 'requests'/'readBefore'/'readAfter': each file analyzed alone as a one-file repo with the built analyzer (eval/dist/usage-lets-analyze.mjs), counting the requests made by a fetch/axios call whose first argument names such a let (matched by name in the file, so a same-named let without += elsewhere in the file counts too), and how many have a read URL: 'readBefore' with this commit's analyzer but += writes rejected as before (lets.ts's old rule), 'readAfter' with the fix. Most unread requests start with a value only known at runtime (this.baseURL, a function's result), which this change doesn't touch. Among the eval checkouts (eval/.repos, every repos.json entry, scanned for let x ... x += in files that request), the form is in batch 5's dotnize/chessu and solid-logic-studios/bucketwise-planner; batch 1's RishiBakshii/mern-ecommerce appends to a let queryString inside .map callbacks, which stays unknown (a write in a nested function).",
